! ax4b_148_immediate_indexed.strap -- jb_ax4b "I-BOX 4", routine 148
! (TEST 5, "CHECKS ALL 8 CODES" of the P field, PDF p.142), the block
! "CHECK INDEXING IMMEDIATE LOAD" that follows TEST 5B ("CHKS P FIELD
! OF 100", PDF pp.143-145):
!
!   PDF p.146  011067.00-011117.40  driver + error entries, bits 0-6
!   PDF p.147  011120.00-011141.40  error entries, bits 7-15
!   PDF p.148  011142.00-011165.40  entries 16-23, exit, continuity
!   PDF p.191  013054.00-013103.00  the common bit table, BIT0-BIT23
!
! The sheets carry NO printed page number (top and foot read on all
! four images), so every line is cited by PDF page and the listing's
! own octal location.  Read from the page images at 150 dpi, the
! driver again at 400 dpi; checked row for row against the printed
! machine code by tests/verify_ax4b_148_immediate_indexed_listing.py
! (149 rows, 8 symbols, all pass).
!
! WHY THIS PAGE.  It is IBM's own test of the rule decks/
! vfl_immediate_indexed.strap had only the Reference Manual for (printed
! p.21, PDF 24: for code 4 "the effective address is used as the
! operand itself"; printed p.56, PDF 59: bits 0-23 are "indexed by ...
! the I field"):
!
!   LI(BU,64,8),0($X3)          0.00 83 400000.20 50      011072.00
!
! "83" is the 1000 tag and I = 3; "400000.20" puts P = 4 (immediate).
! The address field is ZERO, so the operand is purely $X3's value.  The
! loop sets $X3 to BITk's value field (k = 0..23), loads the immediate
! as a 64-bit field (24 bits of EA, zeros to the right: printed p.56,
! "If the field length designated is greater than 24, zeros are added
! to the right"), reads it back through $R into $X3 with LX, and KVs it
! against BITk.  A model that does not index the immediate loads 0 and
! fails on bit 0; one that keeps only the word part of the EA fails on
! bit 18 (both measured, below).
!
! HOW IT WORKS (IBM's code, unchanged):
!   I4841   $X1 walks BIT0..BIT23 (LVI, LCI 24); $X2 walks the error
!           table I4844 in steps of 2.0 words.
!   I48412  SVA $X2 into I4842 ("$B,0"): the failure branch is aimed at
!           bit k's entry.  SVA $X1 into the next half-word: LV,$X3
!           loads BITk.  Both are STORES INTO THE VERY NEXT HALF-WORD
!           the look-ahead may already hold (store-into-prepared).
!   LI ... LX,$X3,$R; SVA $X1 into KV; KV,$X3,BITk; BXE skips I4842.
!   I4843   C-I counts down; BXCZ to I4844A after 24.
!   I4844A  B,$+1.0 jumps OVER "BD,I4841" (the repeat), then SIC,SENO
!           and B,SSW -- back to SSIP.
!
! SUBSTITUTIONS AND SUPPLIED CODE (not on these pages):
!   * SSIP's entry points: SSW (001301.00) is a PASS halt, SERS
!     (001304.00) a FAIL halt, SEN/SENO (001310.00/001311.00) data words
!     SIC stores into.  The addresses are the listing's own (B,SSW
!     prints "1301.10 00" etc.); the contents are SSIP's, which is not
!     transcribed here.  So a failure stops at SERS with SEN naming the
!     entry (the half-word after I4844 + 2k words' SIC).
!   * IC248 is SYN'd from the printed "LX,$X13,IC248" (11306.32 10).
!     The continuity rows after B,SSW are transcribed and verified but
!     never run (SSW halts).
!   * Notation only: the page's "%BU,64,8@" and "%$X3@" are written
!     "(BU,64,8)" and "($X3)"; "%8@" is "(8)"; the label glyph the scan
!     shows as "1" is the letter I (I4841 ...), as for every ax4b label
!     (docs/listing_typography.md).  Nothing else changed.
!
! RESULT ON THE MODEL, 2026-11-18 (dc5331e + this deck): PASSES -- halts
! at SSW (PC 1410, half-words), SEN = 0, $X1 = BIT23's address 013103.00
! with count 0, $X2 = entry 23 (011160.00), $X3's value = BIT23's (.01).
! CYCLES 5946 is MODEL BEHAVIOUR; no time is printed.  IBM's listing and
! the model AGREE: no finding against the model.
!
! INJECTIONS, each in a scratch copy of bsv/ (the worktree untouched),
! the deck run with PC=1410 and SEN=0 pinned -- OBSERVED:
!   CONTROL (the worktree)                 -> PASS, SEN 0
!   A  carryIndex: P = 4 left unindexed     -> halts at SERS (PC 1416);
!      (StretchIBox.bsv, "p == 0 || p == 4"    SEN = 011103.00, the entry
!      -> "p == 0", the pre-fix model)          for BIT 0
!   B  immediateOperand keeps EA bits 0-17  -> halts at SERS (PC 1416);
!      only (bits 18-23 zeroed)                 SEN = 011147.00, the entry
!                                               for BIT 18: bits 0-17 pass
! SEN holds the half-word after the entry's B,SERS (I4844 + 2k + 1.0),
! the return SSIP would take, so it names k exactly.
!
! ---- SSIP's entry points: SUBSTITUTES (not on these pages) -----------
! The addresses are the ones this listing prints for them (SIC,SEN
! "1310.00 80", B,SERS "1304.10 00", SIC,SENO+.32 "1311.40 80", B,SSW
! "1301.10 00"); what is AT them is SSIP's, which this file replaces
! with halts, as ibox4_rnx_run.strap does.
        SLC, (8)1301.0
SSW     BEW, $                        ! SUBSTITUTE: PASS (the return to SSIP)
        SLC, (8)1304.0
SERS    BEW, $                        ! SUBSTITUTE: FAIL (SSIP's error report)
        SLC, (8)1310.0
SEN     DD(BU,64,8), 0                ! SUBSTITUTE: SIC's error link word
SENO    DD(BU,64,8), 0                ! SUBSTITUTE: SIC's other link word
!
! IC248, routine 148's continuity word: SYN from the printed address
! of "LX,$X13,IC248" (11306.32 10); the three continuity rows that
! name it are never reached here (SSW halts first).
IC248   SYN, (8)11306.0
!
! ======================================================================
! PDF p.146, 011067.00-011117.40 (no printed page number on the sheet)
! ======================================================================
        SLC, (8)11067.0
I4841   LVI, $X1, BIT0                ! -CHECK INDEXING IMMEDIATE LOAD.
        LVI, $X2, I4844
        LCI, $X1, 24
I48412  SVA, $X2, I4842
        SVA, $X1, $+.32
        LV,  $X3, 0
        LI(BU,64,8), 0($X3)
        NOP
        NOP
        NOP
        LX,  $X3, $R
        SVA, $X1, $+.32
        KV,  $X3, 0
        BXE, $+1.0
I4842   $B,  0                        ! -FAILURE.
I4843   C-I, $X1, 1                   ! -DONE,
        BXCZ, I4844A                  ! -YES.
        V+I, $X1, 1.0                 ! -NO.
        V+I, $X2, 2.0
        BD,  I48412
        CNOP
!
!                                     ! -YOU CAME TO THIS ERROR TABLE FROM I4842
! error table: PDF p.146 (bits 0-6), p.147 (bits 7-15), p.148 (16-23)
I4844   SIC, SEN                      ! -LD IMMED 0 INDEXED BY BIT 0
        B,   SERS                     ! -FAILED
        B,   I4843                    ! -FAILED
        NOP                           ! -FAILED.
        SIC, SEN                      ! -LD IMMED 0 INDEXED BY BIT 1
        B,   SERS                     ! -FAILED
        B,   I4843                    ! -FAILED
        NOP                           ! -FAILED.
        SIC, SEN                      ! -LD IMMED 0 INDEXED BY BIT 2
        B,   SERS                     ! -FAILED
        B,   I4843                    ! -FAILED
        NOP                           ! -FAILED.
        SIC, SEN                      ! -LD IMMED 0 INDEXED BY BIT 3
        B,   SERS                     ! -FAILED
        B,   I4843                    ! -FAILED
        NOP                           ! -FAILED.
        SIC, SEN                      ! -LD IMMED 0 INDEXED BY BIT 4
        B,   SERS                     ! -FAILED
        B,   I4843                    ! -FAILED
        NOP                           ! -FAILED.
        SIC, SEN                      ! -LD IMMED 0 INDEXED BY BIT 5
        B,   SERS                     ! -FAILED
        B,   I4843                    ! -FAILED
        NOP                           ! -FAILED.
        SIC, SEN                      ! -LD IMMED 0 INDEXED BY BIT 6
        B,   SERS                     ! -FAILED
        B,   I4843                    ! -FAILED
        NOP                           ! -FAILED.
! ---- PDF p.147, 011120.00-011141.40 ----
        SIC, SEN                      ! -LD IMMED 0 INDEXED BY BIT 7
        B,   SERS                     ! -FAILED
        B,   I4843                    ! -FAILED
        NOP                           ! -FAILED.
        SIC, SEN                      ! -LD IMMED 0 INDEXED BY BIT 8
        B,   SERS                     ! -FAILED
        B,   I4843                    ! -FAILED
        NOP                           ! -FAILED.
        SIC, SEN                      ! -LD IMMED 0 INDEXED BY BIT 9
        B,   SERS                     ! -FAILED
        B,   I4843                    ! -FAILED
        NOP                           ! -FAILED.
        SIC, SEN                      ! -LD IMMED 0 INDEXED BY BIT 10
        B,   SERS                     ! -FAILED
        B,   I4843                    ! -FAILED
        NOP                           ! -FAILED.
        SIC, SEN                      ! -LD IMMED 0 INDEXED BY BIT 11
        B,   SERS                     ! -FAILED
        B,   I4843                    ! -FAILED
        NOP                           ! -FAILED.
        SIC, SEN                      ! -LD IMMED 0 INDEXED BY BIT 12
        B,   SERS                     ! -FAILED
        B,   I4843                    ! -FAILED
        NOP                           ! -FAILED.
        SIC, SEN                      ! -LD IMMED 0 INDEXED BY BIT 13
        B,   SERS                     ! -FAILED
        B,   I4843                    ! -FAILED
        NOP                           ! -FAILED.
        SIC, SEN                      ! -LD IMMED 0 INDEXED BY BIT 14
        B,   SERS                     ! -FAILED
        B,   I4843                    ! -FAILED
        NOP                           ! -FAILED.
        SIC, SEN                      ! -LD IMMED 0 INDEXED BY BIT 15
        B,   SERS                     ! -FAILED
        B,   I4843                    ! -FAILED
        NOP                           ! -FAILED.
! ---- PDF p.148, 011142.00-011165.40 ----
        SIC, SEN                      ! -LD IMMED 0 INDEXED BY BIT 16
        B,   SERS                     ! -FAILED
        B,   I4843                    ! -FAILED
        NOP                           ! -FAILED.
        SIC, SEN                      ! -LD IMMED 0 INDEXED BY BIT 17
        B,   SERS                     ! -FAILED
        B,   I4843                    ! -FAILED
        NOP                           ! -FAILED.
        SIC, SEN                      ! -LD IMMED 0 INDEXED BY BIT 18
        B,   SERS                     ! -FAILED
        B,   I4843                    ! -FAILED
        NOP                           ! -FAILED.
        SIC, SEN                      ! -LD IMMED 0 INDEXED BY BIT 19
        B,   SERS                     ! -FAILED
        B,   I4843                    ! -FAILED
        NOP                           ! -FAILED.
        SIC, SEN                      ! -LD IMMED 0 INDEXED BY BIT 20
        B,   SERS                     ! -FAILED
        B,   I4843                    ! -FAILED
        NOP                           ! -FAILED.
        SIC, SEN                      ! -LD IMMED 0 INDEXED BY BIT 21
        B,   SERS                     ! -FAILED
        B,   I4843                    ! -FAILED
        NOP                           ! -FAILED.
        SIC, SEN                      ! -LD IMMED 0 INDEXED BY BIT 22
        B,   SERS                     ! -FAILED
        B,   I4843                    ! -FAILED
        NOP                           ! -FAILED.
        SIC, SEN                      ! -LD IMMED 0 INDEXED BY BIT 23
        B,   SERS                     ! -FAILED
        B,   I4843                    ! -FAILED
        NOP                           ! -FAILED.
I4844A  B,   $+1.0
        BD,  I4841
        SIC, SENO+.32
        B,   SSW                      ! -TO SSIP.
        BD,  $+.32
!
        LX,  $X13, IC248              ! -UPDATE CONTINUITY.
        V+,  $X13, BIT23
        SX,  $X13, IC248
!
! ======================================================================
! PDF p.191, 013054.00-013103.00: the common bit table, BIT0-BIT23
! (the page continues to BIT35; BIT24, a DD, and BIT25 up are not used)
! ======================================================================
        SLC, (8)13054.0
BIT0   XW,  (8)400000.00, 0, 0
BIT1   XW,  (8)200000.00, 0, 0
BIT2   XW,  (8)100000.00, 0, 0
BIT3   XW,  (8)40000.00, 0, 0
BIT4   XW,  (8)20000.00, 0, 0
BIT5   XW,  (8)10000.00, 0, 0
BIT6   XW,  (8)4000.00, 0, 0
BIT7   XW,  (8)2000.00, 0, 0
BIT8   XW,  (8)1000.00, 0, 0
BIT9   XW,  (8)400.00, 0, 0
BIT10  XW,  (8)200.00, 0, 0
BIT11  XW,  (8)100.00, 0, 0
BIT12  XW,  (8)40.00, 0, 0
BIT13  XW,  (8)20.00, 0, 0
BIT14  XW,  (8)10.00, 0, 0
BIT15  XW,  (8)4.00, 0, 0
BIT16  XW,  (8)2.00, 0, 0
